      ],
      "chunk_id": "6b7996bf-697c-4b99-a971-0ab68e9770a8",
      "content": "On-Call Severity Levels\n\n| Severity | Definition | Initial Response Target |\n| --- | --- | ---: |\n| SEV-1 | Widespread production outage or data exposure risk | 15 minutes |\n| SEV-2 | Major workflow unavailable for multiple customers | 30 minutes |\n| SEV-3 | Degraded feature with workaround available | 4 business hours |\n| SEV-4 | Low-impact defect or documentation issue | Next planning cycle |\n\nThe on-call engineer owns triage until an incident commander is assigned. The incident commander owns status updates, escalation, and post-incident review scheduling.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002009",
      "document_id": "ENG-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Manager"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "facb837a-ace7-4994-ae31-1385a5333b0c",
      "content": "Team Planning\n\nManagers should maintain a quarterly team plan with goals, ownership, dependencies, and risks. Plans should identify customer-impacting work, hiring assumptions, and capacity constraints.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002006",
      "document_id": "MGR-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Manager"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "aca897cb-0dd2-4e10-94f2-f3cf9a1ce408",
      "content": "Escalation Paths\n\nEmployee relations concerns should be escalated to People Operations. Security access issues should be escalated to IT Support. Customer-impacting delivery risks should be escalated to the relevant department leader.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002006",
      "document_id": "MGR-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Manager",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "d0cab3f6-9771-40cf-9a66-78a470bb69f7",
      "content": "Deployment Approval\n\n| Change Type | Required Review | Required Approver |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Documentation-only release | Peer review | Team lead |\n| Low-risk application change | Peer review and automated tests | Team lead |\n| Database migration | Peer review, rollback plan, staging proof | Engineering Manager |\n| Security-sensitive change | Peer review, IT Admin review | Engineering Manager |\n| Emergency hotfix | Incident commander review | Engineering Manager on call |\n\nAll production changes must include a rollback plan. A rollback plan that says \"revert if needed\" is not sufficient; it must name the specific revert, migration rollback, feature flag, or mitigation.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002009",
      "document_id": "ENG-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    },
    {
      "access_roles": [
        "Manager",
        "IT/Admin"
      ],
      "chunk_id": "2c2a7311-edec-468a-a9bf-54ef7fc4a28d",
      "content": "Release Windows\n\nStandard production deployments occur Tuesday through Thursday between 10:00 and 15:00 Eastern Time. Deployments outside that window require approval from the Engineering Manager on call and a written reason in the change record.\n\nFriday deployments are limited to severity-one fixes, security patches approved by IT Admin, or customer-impacting incidents where waiting would increase risk. Weekend deployments require the incident commander to approve the change before execution.",
      "department_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002009",
      "document_id": "ENG-001",
      "project_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000019",
      "tenant_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000002801"
    }
  ],
